            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Gujarati for mustard seed, then the Gujarati for cardamom."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ઉમેરવું",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઉમેરવું — umervũ — \"to add\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "તે ચામાં ખાંડ ઉમેરે છે. — te cāmā̃ khā̃ḍ umere che — \"He adds sugar to his tea.\""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ઉમેરવું (umervũ) is a tadbhava. It comes from ummēr, \"join\", a reconstructed form, and CDIAL glosses the Gujarati verb \"to add, augment\" (CDIAL 2347)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for everyday life at A2."
